%% VIS-CL-001 — The Three Post-Senior QA Career Tracks
flowchart TB
    A[Senior QA Engineer] --> B[Individual Contributor Track]
    A --> C[Technical Lead Track]
    A --> D[Management Track]
    B --> B1[Staff / Principal QA Engineer,<br/>QA Architect]
    C --> C1[QA Lead, Test Lead —<br/>technical ownership of the work]
    D --> D1[QA Manager, Head of QA —<br/>ownership of people and outcomes]
    accTitle: The Three Post-Senior QA Career Tracks
    accDescr: Past Senior QA Engineer, a QA career branches into three distinct tracks rather than one ladder. The Individual Contributor track leads to Staff or Principal QA Engineer and QA Architect roles, focused on deep technical work at increasing scope. The Technical Lead track leads to QA Lead and Test Lead roles, owning technical direction for a team's work. The Management track leads to QA Manager and Head of QA roles, owning people and organizational outcomes rather than personal technical output.
